   "definition": "Format a BeatScript program as the editor's fmt button does, in BeatScript 2: one statement a line, one space between tokens, blocks indented two spaces, numbers, notes and chords spelled one way, and the version line `#! beatscript 2` first; the other `#!` header lines, the comments and the blank lines between blocks stay where they are. A BeatScript 1 text (`#! btw 1`, or no version line) is upgraded: the same program under a new CID, and from_cid is the CID of the text as given (the old CID keeps working). Answers text (the formatted program), canonical (the same with no comments and no header lines but the version line: the CID is of that), cid, version (2), from_cid (only when it upgraded) and comments. A BeatScript 2 text formats to its own CID, so use fmt to tidy a program, to upgrade one, or to compare two; eval, load, queue, share and push_private already format what they are given and never upgrade it. A program that does not parse answers the same diagnostics as check. Read-only, no sign-in.",
