   "definition": "Set up a demo recording of a program: the page in record mode (full screen code, the firing markers and follow-scroll on) and the steps that turn it into a video. Give exactly one of text, cid or example (as render does: a text or example is checked and stored publicly as CC0-1.0, nothing private). Answers {cid, seconds, record_url, record_url_manual_clock, audio_url, recipe}. record_url opens the page in record mode and plays it for a person to screen-record; record_url_manual_clock opens it on a fake clock that a script steps frame by frame (window.__btw.setTime(seconds); window.__btw.frame()), which is how site/tools/record-demo.mjs in the repo makes a perfectly synced, stutter-free MP4 (H.264, AAC, 1920x1080) plus a silent hero loop (MP4 and WebM) and a poster PNG, taking the audio from audio_url (the offline render of the same program). This tool does not capture video itself: it needs a browser and ffmpeg on your side. The audio is the offline render: notes and sounds, not control lines (filters, reverb). Call check first. Rendering limits apply (about 30 programs an hour per client). No sign-in needed.",
